// Poolit system architecture, as of 5 Nov 2026
// Diagram type: Cloud architecture diagram (Eraser diagram-as-code)
//
// LEGEND
//   green  = live and checked
//   blue   = built and tested, not switched on yet
//   orange = planned
//   gray   = being retired (week 3 cutover)

title Poolit system architecture
direction right
colorMode bold
styleMode shadow
typeface clean

// ---------------- People ----------------

Students [icon: users, color: green, label: "Students (hostel residents, 18+)"]
Store staff [icon: user, color: green, label: "Store staff (run pools, stock, deliver)"]

// ---------------- Apps ----------------

Apps on Vercel [icon: vercel, color: green] {
  Student app [icon: smartphone, color: green, label: "Student app (React, installable web app)"]
  Vendor console [icon: monitor, color: green, label: "Vendor console (React, phone and desktop, barcode scanner)"]
}

Android app [icon: android, color: orange, label: "Student Android app (Capacitor wrapper, weeks 4 to 5)"]

// ---------------- Old backend ----------------

Express API [icon: server, color: gray, label: "Express API on Vercel (33 routes) retiring in week 3"]

// ---------------- Supabase ----------------

Supabase project [icon: supabase, color: green, label: "Supabase project (Singapore, Free plan)"] {

  Auth [icon: lock, color: green, label: "Auth: phone OTP for students, email and password for vendors"]

  PostgREST [icon: globe, color: green, label: "REST layer: only api functions are reachable, tables are not"]

  Public functions [icon: code, color: green, label: "34 api functions, run as the caller. 8 open to visitors, 26 need sign in"]

  Private helpers [icon: shield, color: green, label: "private schema: access checks and JSON shaping, never reachable from outside"]

  Server only functions [icon: key, color: green, label: "Server only functions: place_order, close_slot, dispatch_slot, restock_item, adjust_stock, ensure_open_slot, barcode generation"]

  Closed tables [icon: database, color: green, label: "11 closed tables: row security on, no grants, no policies"]

  Scheduled jobs [icon: clock, color: green, label: "pg_cron: pool rotation every minute, key cleanup daily"]

  Photo storage [icon: image, color: blue, label: "Bucket product-images: public read, 200 KB cap, WebP or JPEG, vendors may add to their own folder only, no overwrite or delete"]

  Edge Functions [icon: zap, color: orange, label: "Edge Functions: payments, refunds, push notifications"]
}

// ---------------- External services ----------------

External services [icon: cloud, color: orange] {
  SMS provider [icon: message-square, color: orange, label: "SMS provider (DLT registered sender)"]
  Payment gateway [icon: credit-card, color: orange, label: "UPI payment gateway (Phase 2)"]
  Firebase push [icon: bell, color: orange, label: "Firebase Cloud Messaging (free)"]
  Cloudflare [icon: cloudflare, color: orange, label: "Cloudflare: Pages hosting, free picture cache, R2 nightly backup"]
  Monitoring [icon: activity, color: orange, label: "Sentry and uptime check (free tiers)"]
}

// ---------------- Flows: students ----------------

Students > Student app: browse, join pools, order
Students > Android app: later
Student app > Auth: phone OTP sign in
Student app > PostgREST: NEW backend, one call every 15 s (switch VITE_BACKEND, off by default)
Student app > Express API: DEFAULT backend today, also the rollback path
Android app > PostgREST: same calls as the web app
Student app > Photo storage: show pictures (emoji shown if a picture is missing)

// ---------------- Flows: vendors ----------------

Store staff > Vendor console: run pools, restock, deliver, scan barcodes
Vendor console > Auth: email sign in
Vendor console > Express API: orders, stock, pools (not switched yet)
Vendor console > Photo storage: upload one resized picture per product (Add item and Inventory screens)

// ---------------- Inside Supabase ----------------

PostgREST > Public functions: each call runs as visitor or signed in user
Public functions > Private helpers: who is calling, which store, shape the answer
Public functions > Server only functions: only after the caller is checked
Server only functions > Closed tables: atomic changes (stock, orders, pools)
Private helpers > Closed tables: read only lookups
Scheduled jobs > Server only functions: close expired pools, open the next
Express API > Server only functions: service role key, server side only
Express API > Closed tables: service role key, server side only

// ---------------- Planned ----------------

Auth > SMS provider: OTP codes
Student app > Payment gateway: UPI checkout
Payment gateway > Edge Functions: payment confirmation webhook
Edge Functions > Closed tables: mark orders paid, refunds
Edge Functions > Firebase push: order status notifications
Firebase push > Android app: push
Photo storage > Cloudflare: cache pictures once transfer passes 3.5 GB a month
Closed tables > Cloudflare: encrypted nightly backup to R2
Student app > Monitoring: errors
Vendor console > Monitoring: errors
